  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Girish @ Mudalagiriyappa vs Anandakumar on 6 February, 2024 Author: Pradeep Singh Yerur Bench: Pradeep Singh Yerur -1- NC: 2024:KHC:5004 MFA No. 1164 of 2021 IN THE HIGH COURT OF KARNATAKA AT BENGALURU DATED THIS THE 6TH DAY OF FEBRUARY, 2024 BEFORE THE HON'BLE MR JUSTICE PRADEEP SINGH YERUR MISCELLANEOUS FIRST APPEAL NO. 1164 OF 2021 (MV-I) BETWEEN: GIRISH @ MUDALAGIRIYAPPA, S/O RANGAPPA, AGED ABOUT 37 YEARS, RESIDING AT RANGANATHA NAGARA, SIRAT TOWN, NOW RESIDING AT 1ST CROSS, SIRA GATE, TUMAKURU - 572 106. ...APPELLANT (BY SRI. SHANTHARAJ K., ADVOCATE) AND: 1. ANANDAKUMAR, S/O SEEBI RANGAPPA, AGED ABOUT 62 YEARS, Digitally signed R/AT BALAJINAGARA, by V KRISHNA SIRA TOWN - 572 137. Location: High Court of Karnataka 2. UNITED INDIA GENERAL INSURANCE CO. LTD., BY ITS MANAGER, JAYADEVA COMPLEX, B.H. ROAD, 1ST FLOOR, TUMAKURU - 572 101. ...RESPONDENTS (BY SRI. B.A. RAMAKRISHNA, ADVOCATE FOR R2) THIS MISCELLANEOUS FIRST APPEAL IS FILED UNDER SECTION 173(1) OF MV ACT AGAINST THE JUDGMENT AND Girish @ Mudalagiriyappa vs Anandakumar on 6 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/50755120/ 1 AWARD DATED 29.11.2019 PASSED IN MVC NO.56/2019 ON -2- NC: 2024:KHC:5004 MFA No. 1164 of 2021 THE FILE OF THE ADDITIONAL SENIOR CIVIL JUDGE AND MACT.XI, TUMAKURU, PARTLY ALLOWING THE CLAIM PETITION FOR COMPENSATION AND SEEKING ENHANCEMENT OF COMPENSATION. THIS APPEAL, COMING ON FOR ADMISSION, THIS DAY, THE COURT DELIVERED THE FOLLOWING: JUDGMENT",
    "facts": "Hence, the appellant seeks enhancement of compensation. 2. The driver of the said bus drove the vehicle in a rash and negligent manner so as to endanger human life and NC: 2024:KHC:5004 safety, lost control of the vehicle and he applied sudden brake. Due to the said impact, passengers fell down from the seats and the claimant dashed against the iron rod and sustained fractures. Immediately, he was shifted to Government Hospital, Sira, wherein, he was admitted as an inpatient for a period of one week. Thereafter, to Hemavathi Orthopedic and Trauma Center, Tumakuru and he was admitted as an inpatient for a period of 10 days and discharged with an advise to follow up treatment. The claimant spent more than Rs.75,000/- towards treatment, attendant, transport and other expenses. 3.1 It is stated that the claimant was hale and healthy prior to the occurrence of accident, aged about 35 years, he was earning an income of Rs.30,000/- per month by doing carpentry work. Due to the occurrence of accident and injuries suffered, the claimant is unable to do his work normally as he was doing prior to the occurrence of accident. Hence, the claimant filed a claim petition seeking compensation. Hence, sought for dismissal of the claim petition.",
    "arguments": "Being aggrieved by the meager compensation awarded by the tribunal, the claimant is before this Court challenging the impugned judgment and award. Accordingly, he seeks enhancement of compensation. Hence, he seeks dismissal of the appeal."
  },
